WEBVTT

00:02.810 --> 00:08.940
<i>Every story's hero has 
someone they have to fight.</i>

00:10.480 --> 00:12.820
<i>Even in this age where there is no more war...</i>

00:14.000 --> 00:16.260
<i>and in our reality.</i>

00:18.240 --> 00:20.170
Though the world is free of war,

00:20.170 --> 00:26.290
there is a dark place existing in everyone's 
hearts that they do not want seen.

00:27.490 --> 00:30.880
Everyone everywhere.

00:32.140 --> 00:36.270
Those who do not seek the light 
want to take advantage of this.

00:36.750 --> 00:37.630
Shy...

00:38.480 --> 00:39.840
You must understand this.

00:40.450 --> 00:46.070
The duty of a hero is to become 
a beacon of hope for the people,

00:46.840 --> 00:50.730
and to protect the soul of this world.

00:52.050 --> 00:55.470
<i>Right now, the one striking 
fear into our world</i>

00:55.470 --> 00:57.740
<i>has the power to sneak into people's hearts,</i>

00:57.740 --> 01:01.660
<i>uses a ring to make the darkness 
of their emotions lose control,</i>

01:01.660 --> 01:04.790
<i>and turns them into monsters.</i>

01:05.480 --> 01:09.870
<i>Even at my school, Iko 
Koishikawa-san was a target.</i>

01:09.870 --> 01:13.100
This world is full of countless hearts,

01:13.680 --> 01:18.440
but so many of them are 
stuffed into tiny cages.

01:19.000 --> 01:21.130
I'll destroy them all...

01:21.540 --> 01:24.500
All of the cages that keep you hidden.

01:24.890 --> 01:26.810
I mean, just look.

01:28.080 --> 01:31.230
True hearts are just so...

01:32.700 --> 01:34.990
beautiful just as they are.

01:36.970 --> 01:38.140
<i>Stigma...</i>

01:38.880 --> 01:42.130
<i>Just what could his motive be?</i>

01:42.700 --> 01:46.240
<i>And will I be able to fight him...</i>

01:46.620 --> 01:49.820
<i>as a hero who can save people?</i>

01:54.670 --> 01:57.680
Heroes have killed many hearts.

01:58.670 --> 02:02.420
They judge their qualities, lock them away...

02:06.240 --> 02:08.600
The hearts that have nowhere to go anymore

02:09.480 --> 02:11.970
are yearning for the end of this world.

02:13.780 --> 02:18.110
Don't worry. We don't need 
to actually end this world.

02:18.110 --> 02:20.460
We just need to end the heroes.

02:33.400 --> 02:34.290
Now...

02:35.350 --> 02:39.110
Let's return the world to 
how it once was, together.

04:14.980 --> 04:20.360
<b><u>Episode 6
</u> Ice White</b>

04:17.230 --> 04:20.990
Wow, so now you're able to 
use the power of your heart?

04:21.310 --> 04:24.810
Yes. Though not perfectly yet.

04:25.220 --> 04:27.750
Piltz-san also gave me some encouragement...

04:27.750 --> 04:30.740
And I can't keep worrying Pepesha-san.

04:31.040 --> 04:35.250
I need to work even harder 
so I can use it properly.

04:36.780 --> 04:40.000
Piltz-san and Pepesha-san, huh?

04:41.560 --> 04:42.880
Koishikawa-san?

04:42.880 --> 04:46.420
Huh? Oh, er, it's nothing.

04:47.690 --> 04:48.650
<i>Teru.</i>

04:48.650 --> 04:49.760
Shrimpy-san?

04:50.400 --> 04:52.520
<i>We've been summoned by Unilord.</i>

04:53.010 --> 04:55.680
<i>She wants us to come to 
the spaceship immediately.</i>

04:55.680 --> 04:56.770
Understood.

04:57.130 --> 04:59.390
Koishikawa-san, I'm sorry.

04:59.390 --> 05:01.880
It's okay. You must have hero work.

05:01.880 --> 05:04.820
I'll be right here cheering 
for you, Momijiyama-san.

05:13.340 --> 05:16.140
You've got this, Momijiyama-san.

05:21.720 --> 05:25.840
We've received an emergency request to 
mobilize from an international organization.

05:26.560 --> 05:29.220
We do not have further details.

05:30.300 --> 05:35.100
I need you two to immediately head to 
the location and investigate the situation.

05:35.460 --> 05:36.690
Oho...

05:36.690 --> 05:38.980
Just the two of us?

05:39.250 --> 05:44.440
No. You will be meeting with another 
hero who has already headed there.

05:44.440 --> 05:48.740
<i>There's another one?
I-I hope it's someone I know.</i>

05:49.150 --> 05:52.580
The place you will be traveling 
to is the North Pole.

05:52.580 --> 05:53.120
Huh?!

05:53.540 --> 05:56.580
The North Pole?! But why...

05:56.580 --> 06:00.630
There are research groups from many 
countries stationed at the North Pole.

06:01.170 --> 06:04.340
We can speculate that an incident 
happened involving them,

06:04.950 --> 06:07.420
but there are no countries in the North Pole.

06:08.170 --> 06:11.820
And that's why you need 
help from us heroes.

06:11.820 --> 06:13.640
Did I guess that right?

06:14.240 --> 06:16.710
Spirit... and Shy.

06:17.380 --> 06:21.650
Your mission is to resolve this 
problem as quickly as possible.

06:22.170 --> 06:23.400
If you cannot...

06:25.260 --> 06:26.860
You get no snacks.

06:30.810 --> 06:35.740
I'm joking. You may have your 
snacks. Please laugh now...

06:46.480 --> 06:51.020
I-It's so cold... This is... the N-North Pole?

06:51.020 --> 06:53.300
Let's get all the details from the base.

06:53.940 --> 06:56.690
You're cold, Teru-chan? You okay?

06:56.680 --> 06:59.810
<b>Arctic Base</b>

06:56.690 --> 06:59.190
Wait, are you <i>not</i> cold?

07:01.340 --> 07:03.400
Hey, you there!

07:03.670 --> 07:05.900
If you sleep here, you're gonna die!

07:07.340 --> 07:08.770
Hey!

07:08.770 --> 07:11.160
It's cold... I'm tired...

07:11.660 --> 07:14.210
It's cold... I'm tired...

07:16.400 --> 07:17.910
Oh, dear...

07:18.680 --> 07:21.030
Fell asleep in a place like this?

07:21.030 --> 07:24.540
Ah, Spirit. Yes. Do something about this!

07:26.730 --> 07:28.550
Spirit?

07:29.270 --> 07:32.550
Hello? Time to wake up.

07:38.540 --> 07:40.520
Good morning, you two.

07:40.520 --> 07:42.880
This is the first time 
I'm meeting you, Shy-san.

07:42.880 --> 07:45.380
I'm China's hero, Mianlong.

07:45.860 --> 07:48.070
<b>Mianlong
China's Hero
Real name: Mingming Li</b>

07:48.670 --> 07:50.360
It's a pleasure to meet you.

07:50.360 --> 07:52.500
Yes, likewise.

07:52.500 --> 07:56.030
I'm sorry you had to witness 
that embarrassing sight.

07:57.050 --> 08:00.870
So I guess the hero that got 
here earlier was you, Mianlong.

08:01.490 --> 08:04.900
You know, I haven't had 
any Shaoxing wine lately.

08:04.900 --> 08:07.010
Maybe I'll stop by China on my way back.

08:09.170 --> 08:11.910
Could I talk about the mission first?

08:11.910 --> 08:12.640
Oh?

08:14.690 --> 08:19.140
The emergency signal came from 
200 kilometers northeast of here.

08:19.720 --> 08:24.250
It appears as though the research 
vessel <i>Dimitri</i> hit a large ice floe,

08:24.250 --> 08:26.650
but we haven't been able 
to contact them since.

08:27.160 --> 08:29.320
This may be a race against time.

08:29.320 --> 08:31.870
Please accompany us on this rescue.

08:31.870 --> 08:32.900
Roger!

08:33.360 --> 08:38.860
<i>Pepesha-san's usually drunk, but it seems 
like she's on her game when it really matters.</i>

08:38.860 --> 08:41.780
<i>I need to work harder as a hero, too.</i>

08:43.000 --> 08:45.540
The rescue helicopter is ready to take off.

08:45.810 --> 08:46.630
Ready!

08:59.810 --> 09:02.010
<i>Stare...</i>

09:03.740 --> 09:06.060
Um, uh...

09:06.270 --> 09:07.830
<i>I need to find something to talk about...</i>

09:07.830 --> 09:10.360
<i>Since we're at the North Pole...</i>

09:10.360 --> 09:11.150
Hey!

09:12.090 --> 09:15.840
I wanted to talk to you two today.

09:15.840 --> 09:16.720
Huh?

09:16.720 --> 09:18.910
You're both just so amazing...

09:18.910 --> 09:21.030
So I was hoping you'd listen to my concerns.

09:21.410 --> 09:25.290
That's also why I came on this mission...

09:25.620 --> 09:30.570
P-Pepesha-san's one thing, but I'm, uh...

09:30.570 --> 09:32.980
What are you being all serious for?

09:32.980 --> 09:34.550
Did you not get enough sleep?

09:35.270 --> 09:37.800
I mean, I didn't, but...

09:38.900 --> 09:41.050
You see, the other day...

09:41.050 --> 09:43.120
Stigma appeared in my country, too.

09:44.060 --> 09:46.540
The situation was dealt with, but...

09:47.670 --> 09:50.440
<b>Public Disturbance in China
Several Injured</b>

09:47.670 --> 09:50.440
Footage: Viewer

09:48.500 --> 09:49.850
<i>That one news story...</i>

09:50.850 --> 09:56.530
Shy-san, I heard you were able 
to get by without fighting Stigma.

09:57.040 --> 10:00.440
The truth is... I'm not good at fighting.

10:01.490 --> 10:05.560
I'm told all the time that 
heroes need to fight,

10:05.560 --> 10:09.790
but I'd rather just save people 
without fighting bad guys.

10:10.450 --> 10:13.200
Is it cowardly to think that way?

10:13.200 --> 10:15.500
Is that not manly?

10:16.080 --> 10:17.050
Um...

10:17.310 --> 10:20.710
I do think that at times, too.

10:20.710 --> 10:24.060
But it doesn't matter if that's manly or not.

10:24.540 --> 10:25.140
I mean...

10:25.420 --> 10:27.230
you're a girl, anyway!

10:27.230 --> 10:29.730
Gloom...

10:27.700 --> 10:29.730
<i>Gloom...</i>

10:31.320 --> 10:32.730
Huh? What?!

10:33.700 --> 10:34.720
Teru-chan.

10:34.720 --> 10:37.240
Pepesha-san! Huh?! Um...

10:37.810 --> 10:42.680
It's very rude of you to 
assume someone's gender.

10:42.680 --> 10:44.310
Assume?

10:45.200 --> 10:49.290
I-I'm so sorry! You just have 
such a cute face that I...

10:49.980 --> 10:52.510
Teru-chan, now you're just 
rubbing salt in the wound.

10:56.780 --> 10:58.760
We're nearing the location of the signal.

11:02.620 --> 11:05.100
Rescue squad here. Rescue squad here.

11:05.100 --> 11:09.270
Come in, <i>Dimitri</i>. Come in, <i>Dimitri</i>.

11:11.100 --> 11:12.670
We're not getting an answer.

11:12.670 --> 11:16.020
Is it because they can't answer or 
they just didn't get the message?

11:16.900 --> 11:19.280
Wait... Something's wrong.

11:19.890 --> 11:22.030
The sea ice is in strange shapes...

11:22.280 --> 11:24.280
Wow! That's amazing!

11:24.280 --> 11:27.020
I never knew the North 
Pole had ice like that!

11:27.020 --> 11:28.790
Er, no, we've never seen it like tha—

11:31.680 --> 11:33.040
Teru-chan! Mianlong!

11:33.450 --> 11:34.750
Get everyone aboard to safety!

11:42.060 --> 11:43.640
Wh-What...

11:44.450 --> 11:46.630
What just happened?

11:49.680 --> 11:53.400
Ah, it's cold... It's so cold.

11:55.280 --> 11:57.690
Such a warm-looking heart...

11:58.100 --> 11:58.860
Who are you?!

12:00.380 --> 12:03.090
I wonder... If I destroy it...

12:03.790 --> 12:06.020
Will I become warm, too?

12:08.210 --> 12:08.700
Huh?

12:22.220 --> 12:23.100
Oh, dear.

12:27.180 --> 12:28.760
Caught you!

12:29.300 --> 12:31.610
Are you one of Stigma's victims?

12:31.610 --> 12:34.390
Don't worry. I'll—huh?

12:37.280 --> 12:38.200
Hey!

12:38.200 --> 12:39.520
Victim?

12:40.150 --> 12:44.500
You're not supposed to assume what's 
in people's hearts and hold them down

12:44.500 --> 12:46.440
to the point you kill them completely.

12:46.440 --> 12:47.280
What?

12:47.750 --> 12:50.290
Weren't you ever taught that as a child?

12:54.960 --> 12:56.080
P-Pepesha-san?!

12:57.950 --> 12:59.840
Aw, she got my hat.

12:59.840 --> 13:02.230
Th-Thank goodness you're safe.

13:02.230 --> 13:05.090
Teru-chan, she may be a wee 
bit difficult to deal with.

13:05.840 --> 13:08.970
She doesn't have a ring on.

13:09.580 --> 13:10.280
Huh?!

13:18.770 --> 13:19.580
Shy.

13:21.530 --> 13:24.990
<u>Stigma
Nationality:              
 Likes:
A mysterious boy who wants to 
free all the hearts in the world.</u>

13:25.770 --> 13:29.310
She doesn't have a ring on? 
Wh-What does that mean?

13:29.310 --> 13:31.260
Isn't this Stigma's doing?

13:31.260 --> 13:33.500
That's what I thought, too...

13:33.800 --> 13:36.940
But it looks like this will be much 
more troublesome than we thought.

13:37.730 --> 13:40.580
Mianlong, take care of 
the people from the base.

13:40.580 --> 13:42.250
R-Roger!

13:42.590 --> 13:45.670
Now, then... Teru-chan, 
you'll be providing my support.

13:45.670 --> 13:47.010
R-Right.

13:48.540 --> 13:50.010
<i>Can I really do this, though?</i>

13:50.700 --> 13:52.800
<i>A real battle?</i>

13:53.860 --> 13:56.770
<i>For the first time... I'll be 
using my powers in battle.</i>

13:58.850 --> 13:59.600
Teru-chan!

13:59.860 --> 14:02.900
<i>I don't have time to hesitate!</i>

14:03.200 --> 14:05.400
Okay! Here we go, me!

14:06.000 --> 14:08.150
Wow, how passionate.

14:08.780 --> 14:12.030
Flames... Seems warm.

14:13.440 --> 14:14.870
She fell into the ocean!

14:22.300 --> 14:23.250
It's so cold...

14:24.240 --> 14:26.510
I want to use you to warm up.

14:27.790 --> 14:28.510
Hey...

14:29.130 --> 14:30.280
That's okay, right?

14:35.860 --> 14:38.890
Sorry, but you're going 
to have to settle down.

14:39.590 --> 14:41.690
Now I'm dizzy.

14:41.690 --> 14:42.900
And that hurt.

14:43.510 --> 14:46.340
So, who are you?

14:46.340 --> 14:48.380
What are you doing here?

14:52.640 --> 14:54.900
I'm Tzveta.

14:54.900 --> 14:57.160
I just told to stay here. That's all.

14:57.920 --> 15:00.720
I was told heroes would come here...

15:01.250 --> 15:04.170
And that if I destroyed the 
heroes, I could warm up.

15:05.270 --> 15:10.300
Huh... I see. So this was all a trap?

15:10.600 --> 15:13.110
Teru-chan, contact Unilord immediately!

15:13.110 --> 15:14.420
R-Right!

15:14.420 --> 15:15.810
Huh? Uh, hey, wait!

15:16.000 --> 15:20.000
U-Um, I beg your pardon, 
but may I borrow your radio?

15:20.000 --> 15:22.790
Er, well, the helicopter blew up 
along with everything in it.

15:22.790 --> 15:24.470
O-Oh, right!

15:24.470 --> 15:28.140
H-How do I get a hold of Unilord-san?

15:28.570 --> 15:32.500
You should be able to contact her with 
your Heart-shift bracelets, right?

15:32.500 --> 15:33.570
Yup.

15:33.570 --> 15:35.370
O-Oh, that's right!

15:36.620 --> 15:37.580
That girl...

15:38.900 --> 15:40.830
She's been panicking this whole time.

15:41.600 --> 15:43.990
Her face is all red...

15:47.210 --> 15:48.840
She's just like you...

15:49.360 --> 15:50.340
Pesha.

15:50.960 --> 15:51.800
Huh?

16:06.180 --> 16:07.190
Pepesha-san!

16:08.000 --> 16:09.360
Now, then...

16:17.300 --> 16:18.840
How warm...

16:19.620 --> 16:20.720
I like it.

16:22.370 --> 16:26.630
I really like you.

16:28.290 --> 16:30.300
Warm me up even more.

16:36.900 --> 16:38.720
Are you all right, Shy-san?!

16:38.720 --> 16:40.220
S-Sorry!

16:40.760 --> 16:41.830
You're in the way.

16:42.990 --> 16:44.950
Wh-Where's Pepesha-san?

16:44.950 --> 16:46.120
I'm not sure.

16:46.120 --> 16:48.750
But right now, we need to stop her!

16:54.490 --> 16:56.350
<i>That pattern on her cheek...</i>

16:56.350 --> 16:58.210
<i>That wasn't there earlier.</i>

16:58.960 --> 17:01.040
<i>Ever since that appeared on her cheek,</i>

17:01.040 --> 17:03.250
<i>she somehow feels even creepier...</i>

17:04.310 --> 17:07.130
I've decided. I'll kill you first.

17:14.510 --> 17:15.510
Oh, dear.

17:19.510 --> 17:22.100
I guess I shouldn't go near you.

17:24.090 --> 17:25.580
I'm tired now.

17:27.320 --> 17:28.830
Because of you.

17:38.000 --> 17:40.490
Now, all that's left is...

17:50.230 --> 17:52.340
Mianlong-san! Please go!

17:52.660 --> 17:53.510
It's no use.

17:56.470 --> 17:58.890
Dragon's Sleeping Fist Heart-shift Style...

17:56.470 --> 17:58.890
<b>Dragon's Sleeping Fist</b>

17:57.680 --> 17:58.890
<b>Heart-shift Style</b>

18:04.810 --> 18:06.890
<b>Slumbering Claws</b>

18:05.010 --> 18:06.130
Slumbering Claws!

18:12.280 --> 18:16.610
What was that supposed to be? 
That didn't hurt at... all...

18:16.870 --> 18:17.490
Oh?

18:20.020 --> 18:26.190
I'm not... sure why... 
but I'm really sleepy...

18:27.520 --> 18:31.910
My Slumbering Claws aren't 
meant to hurt anyone.

18:31.910 --> 18:34.970
We're going to have you take a little nap.

18:34.970 --> 18:35.880
Mianlong-san!

18:36.490 --> 18:38.660
You did it! That was amazing!

18:38.660 --> 18:41.640
Oh, no! It was all thanks 
to your assistance, Shy-san.

18:42.160 --> 18:43.670
She was a very tough opponent.

18:44.430 --> 18:46.640
Hey! Are you all right?

18:47.130 --> 18:49.000
That's right! Pepesha-san!

18:49.000 --> 18:50.540
Is she inside that ice?

18:50.540 --> 18:51.900
Shy-san! Melt the ice.

18:51.900 --> 18:53.060
R-Right!

19:00.000 --> 19:05.520
<i>But... what did she mean when she said 
she'd warm up if she destroyed the heroes?</i>

19:06.270 --> 19:10.370
<i>Is she really affiliated with Stigma?</i>

19:11.540 --> 19:12.320
Wha?!

19:14.950 --> 19:18.380
Aw... I guess you fell asleep.

19:19.220 --> 19:20.720
But don't worry.

19:21.200 --> 19:23.190
You've already awakened.

19:24.440 --> 19:25.390
Stigma?!

19:26.980 --> 19:29.130
Yes, I'm Stigma.

19:29.700 --> 19:31.980
That's the name you all gave me.

19:32.700 --> 19:34.840
Names are wonderful.

19:35.580 --> 19:38.480
You can feel loved when someone 
calls you by your name.

19:39.080 --> 19:41.490
You can feel like you're there.

19:43.270 --> 19:44.950
She's Tzveta-chan.

19:45.760 --> 19:47.500
That's Weepy-kun.

19:48.080 --> 19:50.250
I gave them those names.

19:50.850 --> 19:53.000
And you're Mianlong-kun.

19:53.000 --> 19:55.290
What an adorable name.

19:55.290 --> 19:56.750
I almost want to eat you right up.

20:01.090 --> 20:06.010
Stigma... I won't let you get 
away with this... any longer.

20:06.870 --> 20:09.040
Yup, Spirit-san.

20:09.580 --> 20:11.770
You're as airy as ever.

20:12.630 --> 20:16.570
Well, I'm done here, so bye-bye.

20:16.570 --> 20:20.320
W-Wait, Stigma! That girl...

20:20.630 --> 20:21.750
Oh, right.

20:22.160 --> 20:25.290
I guess I'll give us a name, too.

20:28.960 --> 20:31.380
I wonder what it should be.

20:32.820 --> 20:37.350
Something that's easy to 
remember... but also mysterious.

20:38.710 --> 20:44.050
No matter the era, it'll be the 
same thing, the same form...

20:45.550 --> 20:48.020
So that you'll all love it.

20:49.440 --> 20:51.560
So that'll it'll forever 
stay in your heart...

20:58.350 --> 21:00.410
We are Amarariruku.

21:02.560 --> 21:04.260
"The ones who dream."

21:06.200 --> 21:08.320
We'll see each other again soon.

21:09.050 --> 21:11.830
Goodnight, heroes.

21:18.400 --> 21:19.510
Stigma...

21:20.810 --> 21:22.460
What are you...

23:00.940 --> 23:02.360
<b>Extra</b>

23:02.360 --> 23:04.480
Inside 
the
 helicopter

23:02.610 --> 23:04.480
<b>Ba Ba Ba BA</b>

23:03.730 --> 23:04.480
<b>Mianlong-san.</b>

23:04.860 --> 23:10.490
<b>If possible, 
I'd like to save
 everyone</b>

23:06.360 --> 23:10.490
<b>without 
fighting 
bad guys.</b>

23:07.860 --> 23:10.490
<b>You, too,
 Shy-san?</b>

23:08.990 --> 23:10.490
<b>I think
 we'll get 
along great.</b>

23:10.490 --> 23:13.990
<b>Yes...</b>

23:12.070 --> 23:13.990
<b>And...</b>

23:14.330 --> 23:18.750
<b>I don't 
want to 
go out
 in public.</b>

23:15.660 --> 23:18.750
<b>And 
interviews 
are scary.</b>

23:16.990 --> 23:18.750
<b>I'm not 
good at 
announcing myself
 like Piltz-san.</b>

23:18.750 --> 23:20.580
<b>Impossible...</b>

23:20.580 --> 23:21.830
